# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Music ignore list (EXAMPLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A "do not warn me about this" list for your music library. Anything you put
# here gets silently dropped from output/music/warnings.json on every run.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy this file to `ignored/music.yaml` (drop the `.example` suffix).
#      The real `music.yaml` is gitignored so your personal decisions don't
#      end up in version control.
#   2. Add path prefixes below — one per line.
#   3. Re-run `npm run music`. Matching warnings disappear from the output.
#
# Two entry shapes — pick whichever fits each case:
#
#   # 1. Path-only (a bare string) — silences EVERY warning under this path.
#   - Music/2Pac/All Eyez on Me
#
#   # 2. Type-scoped (an object) — silences only the listed warning types
#   #    under this path. Other warnings on the same path stay visible.
#   - path: Music/2Pac/All Eyez on Me
#     types:
#       - warn_compilation_detected
#
# Matching is case-insensitive and forward-slash-normalized, so the same
# file works on Windows (backslashes) and macOS/Linux (forward slashes).
#
# Get the paths to add from output/music/warnings.json. Most music warnings
# use a `<Category>/<Artist>/<Album>` path shape (or `<Artist>/<Album>` if
# you don't use category subfolders). Get the warning types from the `type`
# field of each entry, or from rules/music.yaml under `checks`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Silence a whole artist
# (Useful when an artist's catalog has a known issue you've decided to keep —
# e.g. a folder/tag mismatch you can't fix because the tag was set by the
# original publisher.)
# - Some Artist
# - Various Artists


# Silence one album
# (Drops every warning under this album folder — compilation_detected,
# folder_tag_mismatch, missing_tags, track_number_mismatch, etc.)
# - Pink Floyd/The Wall
# - 2Pac/All Eyez on Me


# Silence one track
# (Pin-point: just one file.)
# - Pink Floyd/The Wall/01 - In the Flesh.flac


# Silence a whole category folder
# (Drops EVERY warning under this folder.)
# - Other Music
# - Other Soundtracks


# Silence one warning type for a specific path
# (Most precise option. The example below acknowledges a known hip-hop
# false-positive on compilation detection without silencing other warnings
# on the same album.)
# - path: Music/2Pac/All Eyez on Me
#   types:
#     - warn_compilation_detected
